WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.393
Hi, I'm Juniper!

00:00:02.393 --> 00:00:06.435
Carveout takes a trained Gaussian-splat scene and hands back a list

00:00:06.435 --> 00:00:07.906
of labelled 3D objects.

00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:08.641
Here's how.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.429
The idea: no retraining, and no original photos.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:17.673
Carveout renders its own views, segments them, and lifts every mask back

00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:19.795
onto the Gaussians that drew it.

00:00:21.217 --> 00:00:23.325
Start from a splat you've trained.

00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:28.242
Carveout places synthetic cameras inside a volume you approve, and renders its own views.

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:32.518
SAM three runs a confirmed list of noun phrases over every view,

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:36.053
and logs every raw score, so the thresholds come from data.

00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:38.197
Then the hard part, the lift.

00:00:38.197 --> 00:00:41.932
Each 2D mask is attributed back to the Gaussians that rendered into it.

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:46.461
Out come objects with position, extents, a box and a confidence.

00:00:46.461 --> 00:00:50.943
An optional local vision model can confirm, relabel or reject each one.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:54.927
Say a Gaussian is seen in twenty views.

00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:58.632
Three say salon chair, one says barber chair, sixteen say nothing.

00:00:58.632 --> 00:00:59.643
One rule decides.

00:01:00.063 --> 00:01:03.749
Set every colour to one, render, and multiply by the mask.

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:07.100
The gradient is each Gaussian's share of the masked pixels.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.776
The biggest class total wins.

00:01:09.196 --> 00:01:12.038
T is its mass in every view that saw it.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:15.165
A view that detected nothing is a vote against every label.

00:01:15.585 --> 00:01:17.617
Gamma sets the bar, tuned per class.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.944
The limit is memory.

00:01:20.944 --> 00:01:25.127
The lift needs about twelve bytes per Gaussian per class, so on

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:28.961
a twenty-four gigabyte card, thirty million Gaussians get about sixty classes.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.129
So each view votes with the mass the Gaussian shows in it.

00:01:33.129 --> 00:01:36.159
Large and frontal counts for more than a sliver at the edge.

00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:42.482
To recap: render, detect, then lift each mask by weighted vote.

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:45.470
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:46.080
I'm Juniper.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:46.386
Bye!
